  "created": "2026-11-10T22:06:00.697Z",
  "description": "Data Standardizer provides implementations of various internationally recognised standards in data processing, covering topics ranging from languages to currencies and geographical entities. With strongly-typed enumerations for each standard (where applicable) or other targeted data types, you can represent these elements in your code such that errors with invalid values are minimised.\n\nProvides types supporting the reading and writing of vCard files.  Includes:\n- vCard Format Specification, RFC 6350 (content lines, value types, the card object model, and reading and writing cards with conformance checks)\n- Parameter Value Encoding in iCalendar and vCard, RFC 6868\n- jCard: The JSON Format for vCard, RFC 7095 (reading and writing cards as JSON, on .NET Standard 2.0 and later)\n- xCard: vCard XML Representation, RFC 6351 (reading and writing cards as XML)\n- vCard 2.1 (reading and writing vCard 2.1 cards, with quoted-printable, BASE64, CHARSET, parameters with no name and the card an AGENT holds)\n- vCard MIME Directory Profile, RFC 2426, and MIME Content-Type for Directory Information, RFC 2425 (reading and writing vCard 3.0 cards, and converting between versions)\n- Calendar Attributes for vCard and LDAP, RFC 2739\n- vCard Extensions for Instant Messaging, RFC 4770\n- vCard Format Extensions for JSContact, RFC 9554\n- vCard KIND:application, RFC 6473, and vCard KIND:device, RFC 6869\n- vCard Format Extensions: Place of Birth, Place and Date of Death, RFC 6474\n- vCard Format Extensions: Representing vCard Extensions Defined by the Open Mobile Alliance (OMA) Converged Address Book (CAB) Group, RFC 6715\n- vCard Format Extensions: ICANN Extensions for the Registration Data Access Protocol, RFC 8605",
  "iconFile": "054-doc_web.png",
