  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New:\n- `VcardContentLineReader` reads the content lines of vCard data (RFC 6350 §3.3), with groups and RFC 6868 caret encoding, synchronously or asynchronously, with a zero-copy `VcardContentLineView`.\n- `VcardContentLineWriter` writes the content lines of vCard data, with groups, folding at 75 octets and RFC 6868 caret encoding in vCard 4.0 cards, synchronously or asynchronously, with `IProgress<VcardWriteProgress>`.\n- In a vCard 2.1 card, `VcardContentLineReader` reads parameters with no name, quoted-printable soft line breaks, `BASE64` values ending at an empty line and nested `AGENT` cards, and `VcardContentLineWriter` writes soft line breaks and `BASE64` values.\n- `VcardContentLine` and `VcardContentLineView` decode a value by its `ENCODING` and `CHARSET` with `GetDecodedValue` and `GetDecodedText`, and `LegacySyntax` says which vCard 2.1 features a line uses.\n- `VcardOptions` adds `AcceptLegacySyntax`, `AcceptRfc6350FoldsInVersion21`, `AcceptEightBitWithoutEncoding`, `AllowUnknownCharsetAsLatin1` and `CharsetResolver`.\n- Parse and format vCard values with typed, span-based value types.\n- Read and write vCard 4.0 cards with VcardCard, VcardReader and VcardWriter.\n- Read and write the vCard 4.0 extensions of RFC 6473, RFC 6474, RFC 6715, RFC 6869 and RFC 8605, with typed members on `VcardCard` and `IVcard40Card`.\n- Read and write the vCard 4.0 extensions of RFC 9554, including `CREATED`, `GRAMGENDER`, `LANGUAGE`, `PRONOUNS`, `SOCIALPROFILE` and their parameters, with typed members on `VcardCard` and `IVcard40Card`.\n- Read and write vCard 3.0 cards (RFC 2426, RFC 2739 and RFC 4770) with `VcardReader` and `VcardOptions.WriteVersion`, and view them through `IVcard30Card`.\n- `VcardVersionConverter` lists what a card loses in another version and converts it, and writing data the version can't hold throws unless `AllowLossyVersionConversion` is set.\n- `VcardCard` has `Mailer`, `Classification`, `SourceName`, `Profile`, `CalendarAccessUris` and `Agents` for the properties of older versions.\n- Read and write vCard 2.1 cards, including quoted-printable, `CHARSET`, `BASE64` and the card an `AGENT` holds, with `VcardReader` and `VcardOptions.WriteVersion`, and view them through `IVcard21Card`.\n- `VcardOptions.WriteNamedTypesInVersion21` writes each `TYPE` of a vCard 2.1 card with its name, as `TEL;TYPE=WORK:`.\n- `JcardReader` and `JcardWriter` read and write jCard (RFC 7095), the JSON form of vCard, on .NET Standard 2.0 and later.\n- The date, time, offset, TEXT, BOOLEAN, INTEGER, FLOAT, URI, LANGUAGE-TAG, GEO and PID values parse and format `VcardValueFormat.Json`, the jCard form of their values, on every target.\n- `XcardReader` and `XcardWriter` read and write xCard (RFC 6351), the XML form of vCard, on every target.\n- The date, time, offset, TEXT, BOOLEAN, INTEGER, FLOAT, URI, LANGUAGE-TAG, GEO and PID values parse and format `VcardValueFormat.Xml`, the xCard form of their values.",
